# SushiTrack C/C++ package

A ready-to-link build of the SushiTrack tracker and its C API.

## Contents
```
include/         Public headers (SushiTrack/c_api/sushitrack_c.h)
lib/             Link library ({import_lib})
bin/             Runtime libraries ({runtime_lib}, {sushilog_lib})   [Windows only]
sushitrack.json  Default runtime configuration; edit it to retune without recompiling
example/         A usage example and its CMakeLists.txt
LICENSE          The PolyForm Noncommercial licence of SushiTrack
NOTICE.md        The third-party code inside the libraries
licenses/        The licence texts NOTICE.md cites
```

## Quick start
```sh
cd example
cmake -B build
cmake --build build
```

## Integrating into your own project
- Add `include/` to your include path and include `SushiTrack/c_api/sushitrack_c.h`.
- Link against `lib/{import_lib}`.
- On Windows, keep `bin/{runtime_lib}` and `bin/{sushilog_lib}` on the PATH or beside your executable.
- Create the tracker with `sushitrack_create_tracker("sushitrack.json")` to read the configuration.
- Ship `LICENSE`, `NOTICE.md` and `licenses/` with any copy of the libraries.

Platform: {platform}
